// find the missing number in array

Using a HashSet is significantly better than using JSON for finding a missing element in an array.
A HashSet is a specialized data structure designed for fast lookups, while JSON is a data serialization format meant for transferring data,
 not for algorithmic computations.Here is a direct comparison of both approaches using Java:
 
 import java.util.HashSet;

public class MissingElement {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int[] ar = {1, 2, 3, 1}; // Duplicate '1' means '4' is missing from a 1-4 sequence
        int n = 4; // Expected total elements (1 to 4)
        
        HashSet<Integer> set = new HashSet<>();
        for (int num : ar) {
            set.add(num);
        }
        
        // Find which number from 1 to n is missing
        for (int i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
            if (!set.contains(i)) {
                System.out.println("Missing element: " + i); // Outputs 4
            }
        }
    }
}
